\eqn{j = 1} (see \code{\link[=iv_jlmpv2009]{iv_jlmpv2009()}}).
\item The factor \eqn{A^{-1} = (1 - \psi_1^{k_n}\Delta_n/(2\theta^2
  \psi_2^{k_n}))^{-1}} of \eqn{C_{t,a}} removes the bias
\eqn{-\psi_1\Delta_n IV/(2\theta^2\psi_2)} that the RV-based noise
correction introduces (Section 2.3). \code{bias_factor = TRUE} (default)
applies it to every adjusted estimator:
\itemize{
\item \eqn{BT_{t,a}}: Section 4.1 lists the finite-sample constants and the
summand count and calls the result the "corresponding" estimator; the
